Third-party material
--------------------

sf-save-reader (external/sf-save-reader, a git submodule; sf-save-reader.dll and sf-save-reader.exe in the release zip)
    The save reader, by Richard Bejtlich, under the MIT License (https://github.com/taosecurity/sf-save-reader). Its
    license text is in external/sf-save-reader/LICENSE, and in licenses/sf-save-reader-LICENSE.txt in the release zip.

Libraries (not included in the source; downloaded from nuget.org at build time, and included as DLLs in the release zip)
    Mutagen.Bethesda.Starfield and its Mutagen dependencies (Mutagen.Bethesda.Core, Mutagen.Bethesda.Kernel, Loqui,
        Noggog.CSharpExt), by Noggog and the Mutagen contributors, GPL-3.0 (https://github.com/Mutagen-Modding/Mutagen).
    Taosecurity.Starfield.BuildKit, by Richard Bejtlich, GPL-3.0 (https://github.com/taosecurity/BuildKit).
    Other packages that Mutagen uses (for example GameFinder, K4os.Compression.LZ4, SharpZipLib, System.Reactive,
        ValveKeyValue) each carry their own license, listed on their nuget.org pages.
    The release zip needs the .NET runtime, which is not included (MIT license, https://github.com/dotnet/runtime).

sf-save-health holds no Bethesda game files or game code. It reads the official masters and your mods from your own
game installation when it runs, and it only reads saves.
